hadiths[200]{hadithnumber,text}:
"601","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, says that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""The pens have dried after writing about the fortunate and the unfortunate, and four things have been decided: character, birth, death, and sustenance."
"602","Sayyida Umm Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from Sayyiduna Abu Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him), he says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Allah has already finished (writing) five things for every servant: his deeds, his death, his life, his sustenance, and his abode. No servant can go beyond what Allah has written regarding these.”"
"603","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I submitted, “O Messenger of Allah! Indeed, I am a young, unmarried man, and I fear the trial of desire for myself. Grant me permission to become castrated.” So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whatever is to befall you, the pen has already written it and it has dried, so whether you become castrated or refrain (it will not change anything).”"
"604","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever is going to befall you, the Pen has already written it and it has dried."
"605","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will find the worst among people to be the two-faced one, who comes to these with one face and to those with another face."" Imam Muslim ibn Hajjaj has also narrated it with his chain from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), and in it is: ""Who comes to these with one face and to those with another face."
"606","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will find people like mines (of gold and silver); those who were the best in the pre-Islamic period of ignorance will be the best in Islam, provided they gain understanding of the religion. And in the matter of (leadership), you will find the best among you to be the one who dislikes it the most, until he is involved in it. And you will find the worst among you to be the two-faced person, who comes to these people with one face and to those people with another face."
"607","Sayyiduna Mirdas Aslami (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The righteous people will depart one by one, until only people as worthless as the husks of dates remain; Allah will not care for them at all."
"608","Sayyiduna Mustawrid Fahri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The righteous people will depart one by one, and only worthless people like the husks of dates will remain; Allah will not care about them at all."
"609","Sayyiduna Mustawrid Fahri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The righteous people will depart one by one, and only worthless people like the husks of dates will remain; Allah will not care about them at all."
"610","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One of you sees the speck in his brother's eye but leaves the beam in his own eye."
"611","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sufyan bin Asid Hadhrami (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""The greatest betrayal is that you speak to your brother about something and he believes you to be truthful, while you are lying to him."
"612","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sufyan bin Asid (may Allah be pleased with him) similarly, and he said: ""The greatest betrayal is that you say something to your brother in which he believes you to be truthful, while you are lying to him."
"613","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sufyan bin Asid Hadhrami (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""The greatest betrayal is that you speak to your brother with something in which he believes you to be truthful, while you are lying to him."
"614","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon to us while sitting on his camel Jad‘a, and in his sermon he said: ""O people!........"" and he narrated this hadith."
"615","Sayyiduna Rukb Misri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Glad tidings for the person who adopted humility despite having no defect or fault in himself, considered himself low despite not being poor or needy, spent from the wealth he had gathered without any sin, kept company with people of jurisprudence and wisdom, and showed mercy to the poor and destitute. Glad tidings for the person whose earnings are pure, whose inner self is good, whose outward appearance is excellent, and who kept his evil away from people. Glad tidings for the person who acted upon his knowledge, spent from his surplus wealth, and refrained from unnecessary talk.”"
"616","Sayyiduna Fadala bin Ubaid (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Glad tidings for the person who is guided to Islam, whose livelihood is just sufficient, and who is endowed with contentment.”"
"617","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Fadala bin Ubaid (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""He has succeeded who has been guided to Islam, whose livelihood is sufficient for his needs, and who is content with what he has been given."
"618","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O son of Adam! What you have is sufficient for you, yet you seek that which will make you rebellious. O son of Adam! You are not content with little, nor are you satisfied with much. When you wake up in the morning in a state of physical health, secure regarding yourself and free from fear, and you have your food for the day, then throw dust on the world."
"619","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) that when a petitioner would come to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) or someone would request a need from him, he (peace be upon him) would say: ""Intercede, you will be rewarded, and Allah will decide what He wills through the tongue of His Prophet."
"620","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a petitioner is brought to me and someone asks me regarding a need, and you are present with me, so intercede (recommend) for him; you will be rewarded, and Allah will decide on the tongue of His Prophet whatever He wills."
"621","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he mentioned it briefly, and in it is: ""Intercede, you will surely be rewarded."
"622","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Travel, you will remain healthy and gain spoils."
"623","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith."
"624","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Make things easy, do not make them difficult; give reassurance, do not spread aversion."
"625","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Make things easy, do not make them difficult; give glad tidings, do not spread aversion."
"626","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Adopt moderation and remain upright, for none of you will be saved by his deeds alone."" It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! Not even you? He replied: ""Not even me, unless Allah envelops me in His mercy."
"627","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Adopt moderation and remain upright."" This hadith is concise."
"628","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Adopt moderation, remain upright, and give glad tidings."" This hadith is concise."
"629","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Hurairah! Visit (your Muslim brother) from time to time, love will increase."
"630","It is also narrated in the same manner from Talha bin Amr, may Allah have mercy on him, with his chain, through another chain of transmission."
"631","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith."
"632","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Dharr! Visit (your Muslim brother) from time to time; love will increase."
"633","Sayyiduna Amr bin Umayyah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I asked: O Messenger of Allah! Should I tie my mount and then rely on Allah, or should I leave it untied and rely on Allah? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tie it and then rely (on Allah)."
"634","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Begin (charity and alms) with those whom you support."
"635","Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you test people (when you test them, their inner feelings will become apparent to you, so) you will be compelled to cut off relations with them."
"636","Sayyiduna Abu Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated it as marfu’ from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that: “Test people (when you test them, their inner feelings will become apparent to you, so) you will be compelled to cut ties with them, and place your trust in people gradually.”"
"637","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Preserve knowledge by writing it down."
"638","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying this while he was advising a man: ""O so-and-so! Take little debt and you will remain free, commit few sins and death will be easy upon you, and see and consider where you are placing your seed (for having children), because the vein (of kinship) is a puller (it brings forth the character of the elders in the offspring)."
"639","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Hurairah! ......"" And he narrated this hadith briefly and in it he used the words «واحسن جوار من جارك» instead of «واحسن مجاورة من جارك» ."
"640","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith and in it he said: ""And treat your neighbor well, you will become a (true) Muslim, and laugh less, for excessive laughter deadens the heart."" The correct chain is as follows «عن ابي رجاء من برد بن سنان»"
"641","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)... and he narrated this hadith."
"642","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Huraira! Treat your neighbor well and you will become a (true) Muslim; treat your companion well and you will become a believer; act upon the obligations of Allah and you will become a worshipper; and be content with Allah's distribution and you will become an ascetic."
"643","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) while advising a man said: “Renounce the world and Allah will love you, and be indifferent to what people possess and people will love you.”"
"644","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) took my hand and said: ""Live in this world as if you are a stranger or a traveler, and count yourself among the people of the graves."
"645","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Leave that which causes you doubt for that which does not cause you doubt."" And he mentioned it concisely."
"646","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Help your brother, whether he is an oppressor or oppressed."
"647","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Show mercy to those on the earth, and the One in the heavens will show mercy to you."
"648","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Show gentleness, gentleness will be shown to you."
"649","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Anas! Perform ablution completely, your life will be increased; greet your family, blessings and goodness in your home will increase; greet every person of my Ummah whom you meet, your good deeds will increase; always sleep in a state of purity, for if you die in that state, you will die as a martyr; perform the Duha prayer, for it is the prayer of those who turned to Allah before you; and pray day and night, the guardian angels will protect you; honor the elders, show mercy to the young, you will meet me tomorrow (on the Day of Judgment)."
"650","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Avoid asking (begging) as much as possible."
"651","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I entered the mosque and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sitting alone, so I also sat down with him. I said... and (then) he narrated a long hadith in which it was also mentioned: ""Speak the truth even if it is bitter."
"652","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ...... and he narrated this hadith: ""Fear Allah wherever you are, and follow up a bad deed with a good deed—it will erase it; and behave with good character towards people."
"653","It is narrated from an Ansari man, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Keep your family ties fresh, even if it is only through greeting (salaam)."
"654","Suwaid bin Aamir, may Allah be pleased with him, who was an Ansari companion, says that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Keep your family ties fresh, even if it is only through greeting (salaam)."
"655","It is narrated from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Exchange gifts among yourselves, love will increase between you; migrate, the honor and dignity of your family and children will increase; and overlook the mistakes of honorable people."
"656","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Exchange gifts among yourselves, for a gift removes malice from the heart."
"657","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give gifts to each other, love will be created among you."" (The narrator of the hadith, Abu Shanji, said:) «تحابوا» is with the shaddah on the letter ""ba"", whose root is «حب» , and if it is read with lightness, then it will be derived from «محاباة» . (Meaning to show partiality)"
"658","Abu al-Qasim Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz Baghdawi, may Allah have mercy on him, says that he said to Abu Nasr al-Tammar: While I was listening, did Kawthar bin Hakim narrate to you, on the authority of Mak'hool al-Dimashqi, who was a freed slave of the tribe of Hudhail and was from Kabulistan, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Exchange gifts among yourselves, for the gift removes malice."" Abu Nasr said: Yes."
"659","Sayyida Umm Hakim bint Wada’ Khuzaiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Exchange gifts among yourselves, for this increases love and removes malice from the hearts.”"
"660","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Exchange gifts among yourselves, for gifts remove enmity."
"661","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek goodness and virtue near those with beautiful faces."
"662","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Convey from me (what you hear), even if it is only one verse, and narrate from the Children of Israel, there is no harm."
"663","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Beware of the insight of the believer, for he sees with the light of Allah."
"664","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of unlawful wealth in construction, for it is the root of corruption."
"665","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Honor your children and teach them good manners."
"666","It is narrated from Sayyiduna ‘Ubādah bin Sāmit (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Speak good words and you will benefit, and remain silent from bad words and you will be safe.”"
"667","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Choose (the best) women for your offspring."
"668","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Remember frequently the destroyer of pleasures (death), for indeed, whenever a servant remembers it in hardship, it brings him ease, and whenever he remembers it in ease, it brings him hardship."
"669","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)...... and he narrated this hadith."
"670","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remember frequently the destroyer of pleasures (death)."" And while narrating it, he said: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and narrated it."
"671","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Remember frequently the destroyer of pleasures (death), for indeed, if it is remembered in abundance of wealth, it diminishes it, and if it is remembered in scarcity of wealth, it increases it.”"
"672","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(When you feel weariness) give your hearts comfort for a while."
"673","Sayyiduna Usama bin Umair (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wear the turban, it will increase you in forbearance."
"674","Mus'ab bin Sa'd (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from his father that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) also said this in a hadith and he narrated it: ""Keep doing deeds, for every person is made easy the deeds for which he was created."
"675","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Marry a loving and fertile woman, for I will boast of your numbers before other nations.”"
"676","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Partake in suhoor, for there is blessing in suhoor."" Imam Muslim has also narrated it with his chain from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) as a marfu' narration."
"677","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Partake in suhoor, for there is blessing in suhoor."
"678","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Protect yourselves from (the) Fire, even if it be with half a date."
"679","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Protect yourselves from the Fire, even if it be with half a date."" This hadith is rare among the narrations of Imam Malik. Abu Muhammad Tajibi informed us that indeed Abu Muhammad Abdul Ghani bin Sa'id al-Hafiz wrote it from him."
"680","Abu Bahr Bakrawi (may Allah have mercy on him) says: We were with Imam Shu’bah when a beggar came, so Shu’bah said: Give charity. But the people did not give charity, so he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us from Abdullah bin Ma’qil from ‘Adi bin Hatim that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Save yourselves from the Fire, even if it is with half a date.” (Even after hearing the hadith) nothing was given to the beggar, so Imam Shu’bah said: Al-A’mash narrated to us from Khaythamah from ‘Adi bin Hatim that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Save yourselves from the Fire, even if it is with half a date.” Even this time, the people did not give anything (to the beggar), so Imam Shu’bah said: Muhall bin Khalifah narrated to us, he said: I heard ‘Adi bin Hatim say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Save yourselves from the Fire, even if it is with half a date.” The narrator says that even then the people did not give anything, so Imam Shu’bah said: By Allah! Today I will keep narrating some hadith to you, you miserly shopkeepers! Get up and leave from here."
"681","Sayyiduna ‘Adi bin Hatim (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say... and he narrated this hadith."
"682","Sayyiduna ‘Adi bin Hatim (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Save yourselves from the Fire, even if it is with half a date.”"
"683","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with both of them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Protect yourselves from the Fire, even if it be with a piece of date.” Imam Dar Qutni said: Ibn Munabbih told us: I do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith from Simak bin Harb except Ayyub bin Jabir. And he (Ayyub) is the brother of Muhammad bin Jabir Sahimi; it is said that he is more reliable than his brother Muhammad bin Jabir."
"684","Sayyiduna ‘Adi bin Hatim (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)... and he narrated this hadith."
"685","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... And he narrated this hadith. And Imam Muslim has narrated it with his chain from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that: ""Beware of miserliness, for it destroyed those before you."
"686","This narration is also reported through another chain from Husayn al-Ju'fi, may Allah have mercy on him, with his chain in the same manner."
"687","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be independent of people, even if it is in the matter of a miswak (tooth-stick)."
"688","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be independent of people, even if it is in the matter of a miswak (tooth-stick)."
"689","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Muslamah bin Makhlad (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said this statement. And in Hashimi’s narration, it is that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said this statement: “Give women sufficient clothing so that they may remain settled in their homes.”"
"690","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon on the Day of Sacrifice at Mina during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he mentioned a long sermon of the Prophet in which he also stated: ""Accept the advice of goodness regarding women, for they are captives with you."
"691","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith: ""Protect your wealth through zakat, treat your sick through charity, and confront calamity through supplication."
"692","Zaid bin Aslam says that my father recited (the Qur'an) before the Prophet (peace be upon him), and those (people) were overcome with emotion. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith: ""Consider the time of being overcome with emotion as an opportunity for supplication, for it is mercy."
"693","Sayyiduna Rabi’ah bin ‘Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated it: “(In your supplications) be frequent in saying ‘Ya Dhal-Jalali wal-Ikram.’”"
"694","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek sustenance in cultivation."
"695","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, and she narrated this hadith."
"696","Sayyida Umm Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from Sayyiduna Abu Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him), who says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said—and he narrated it concisely: “As much as possible, remain free from the worries of the world.”"
"697","Sayyiduna Miqdam bin Ma'dikarib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, and he narrated this hadith: ""Measure your grain, there will be blessing in it for you."
"698","Sayyiduna Miqdam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Measure your grain, there will be blessing for you."
"699","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, and he narrated this hadith."
"700","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah says: “Seek goodness and virtue from among My servants who are merciful; live under their shade, for My mercy is with them. And do not seek this goodness and virtue from those whose hearts are hard, for My displeasure is with them.” ‘Abd al-Ghaffar bin Hasan bin Dinar is alone in narrating this hadith, and he is considered weak in hadith."
"701","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Always seek goodness and virtue, and pursue the fragrant breezes of Allah the Exalted’s mercy. Indeed, Allah the Exalted sends the fragrant breezes of His mercy to whichever of His servants He wills. And ask Allah that He conceals your faults and keeps you safe and secure from the things you fear."
"702","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you perform ablution in a vessel, do not lift the water vessel until it is filled, and collect the water of ablution; Allah will rectify your disordered affairs."
"703","Sayyiduna Rafi‘ bin Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, and he narrated this hadith: “Offer the Fajr prayer when it is well-lit, for it is greater in reward.”"
"704","Sayyiduna Salman al-Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Perform tayammum with the earth, for it is compassionate towards you like a mother."" Imam Tabarani said: Only Faryabi has narrated it from Sufyan al-Thawri."
"705","Abu Uthman Nahdi (may Allah have mercy on him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform tayammum with the earth, for it is compassionate towards you like a mother."
"706","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, and he narrated it concisely: ""Leave the people (free); Allah Almighty provides sustenance to some through others."
"707","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek help in fulfilling your needs by keeping them secret, for every person who is blessed is envied."
"708","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek help in fulfilling your needs by keeping them secret, for every person who is blessed is envied."
"709","Sayyiduna Rafi‘ bin Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Before buying a house, look for a good neighbor, and before traveling, look for a good companion.”"
"710","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, and he narrated this hadith: ""Seek treatment, for the One who has sent down the disease has also sent down the cure."
"711","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that a man came and began to praise Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him). Sayyiduna Miqdad (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and began to throw dust on his face. Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: ""What has happened to you?"" He replied: ""I cannot leave what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say,"" and then he narrated this hadith:"
"712","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “When leadership is entrusted to you, deal well and show leniency to your subjects.”"
"713","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Feed your food to the pious people and do good to the believers."
"714","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)...... and he narrated this hadith."
"715","Sayyiduna Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that indeed he (peace be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith: ""Seek refuge with Allah from that greed which leads to the sealing of hearts."
"716","Sayyiduna Abu Humayd Sa‘idi (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Adopt a good method for acquiring worldly means, for every person’s actions are made easy for that which he was created.”"
"717","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Set your worldly affairs right and act for your Hereafter as if you are going to die tomorrow."
"718","Sayyiduna Bara’ bin ‘Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith: “Spread the greeting of peace, you will remain safe.”"
"719","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Salam (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived in Madinah, people began to come to him in groups, so I was also among those who came to him. When I saw his face, I realized that this is not the face of a liar. I heard him say: ""O people! Spread peace (salam) widely, feed (others), maintain ties of kinship, and pray at night when people are asleep; you will enter Paradise in peace."
"720","Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take care regarding my Companions, for indeed they are the best people of my Ummah."
"721","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)...... and he reported this hadith: ""Take care of my 'itrah (my close relatives) for my sake."
"722","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard Sayyiduna Abul Qasim (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Seek guidance from the intelligent, you will find guidance, and do not disobey them, otherwise you will regret."
"723","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon to us on Friday and said: ""Turn to your Lord in repentance before you die, and perform righteous deeds before you become occupied, and strengthen your relationship with Him by remembering Him abundantly."
"724","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said from the pulpit: ""O people! Turn to your Lord before death comes to you, and hasten to do good deeds before you become occupied, and strengthen your relationship with Him by remembering Him abundantly and by giving charity openly and secretly, which is between you and Him. You will be helped, you will be rewarded, and you will be provided for."" This hadith is concise."
"725","Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When it is not a matter of a prescribed legal punishment, then refrain from punishing people of dignity."
"726","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Overlook the slip of a generous person, for whenever he stumbles, Allah is the One who takes hold of his hand."
"727","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Visit the sick, attend funerals; (doing so) will remind you of the Hereafter."
"728","It is narrated from Sa'id bin al-Musayyib and Mawraq 'Ajli that Sayyiduna Sa'd bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with them both) and Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them both) went to visit Sayyiduna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) when he was ill. Salman began to weep, so they said to him: O Abu 'Abdullah! What has made you weep? He said: This covenant which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) took from us, but none of us has fulfilled it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said . . . . . and he narrated: ""Each of you should have in this world only as much provision and share as a rider carries in his journey."
"729","Amr bin Maymun Awdi, may Allah have mercy on him, says that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, while advising a person, said: ""Consider five things as valuable before five things: your youth before your old age, your health before your illness, your wealth before your poverty, your free time before your busyness, and your life before your death."
"730","Ibn Aisha narrates from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) once said while delivering a sermon: ""A servant should take provisions for himself from his own self, for his Hereafter from his worldly life, from his youth before his old age, and from his life before his death, for after this world there is no home except either Paradise or Hell."
"731","Sayyiduna Hakam bin Umair Thamali رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم said: ""Live in this world as a guest, make the mosques your home, accustom your hearts to tenderness and gentleness, frequently reflect and weep, and let not desires cause discord within you."
"732","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Honor the witnesses, for Allah, through them, grants the rights of those entitled and, by their means, prevents oppression."
"733","Sayyiduna Khuzaymah bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of the supplication of the oppressed, for it is raised above the clouds. Allah Almighty says: By My honor and majesty! I will surely help you, even if it is after some time."
"734","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Have mercy on three types of people: a wealthy person of a community who has become poor, a person of honor who has become humiliated, and a scholar with whom foolish and ignorant people are making fun and playing games."
"735","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take dinner, even if it is only a handful of inferior dates, for abandoning dinner causes old age."
"736","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Look at those who are below you and do not look at those who are above you, because this is more appropriate so that you do not consider any blessing of Allah upon you as insignificant."
"737","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Look at those who are below you and do not look at those who are above you, for this is more appropriate so that you do not consider any of Allah's blessings upon you as insignificant."
"738","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith: ""Remove harmful things from the path of the Muslims; your good deeds will increase."
"739","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Love your friend to a certain extent only, for it is possible that one day he may become your enemy; and hate your enemy to a certain extent only, for it is possible that one day he may become your friend."
"740","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""I advise you to adopt the fear of Allah, for it is the foundation of your deeds, and make jihad obligatory upon yourself, for it is the monasticism of my ummah. And what you know about yourself (your faults, etc.) should prevent you from (speaking ill of) people, and keep your tongue restrained except for saying good, for by doing so you will overcome Satan."
"741","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one whose knowledge does not benefit him, his ignorance will harm him. Recite the Qur'an, for it will prevent you (from evil); if it does not prevent you, then (it is as if) you have not recited it at all."
"742","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Return the trust to the one who entrusted you, and do not betray the one who betrayed you."
"743","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said... and he narrated this hadith."
"744","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pay the laborer his wages before his sweat dries."
"745","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O boy! Guard (the commands of) Allah, Allah will guard you. Guard (the rights of) Allah, you will find Him before you. Recognize Him in times of ease, He will recognize you in times of hardship. And know that whatever has reached you could not have missed you, and whatever has missed you could not have reached you. And know that if all of creation were to gather together to benefit you with something that Allah has not decreed for you, they would not be able to do so. Or if they were to gather to harm you with something that Allah has not decreed for you, they would not be able to do so. And when you ask, ask Allah. And when you seek help, seek help from Allah. And know that indeed help comes with patience, relief comes with affliction, and with hardship comes ease. And know that whatever is to happen, the pen has already written it.”"
"746","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d Sa’idi (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: “O Muhammad! Live as long as you wish, in the end you will have to die. Love whomever you wish, in the end you will have to part from them. And do whatever deeds you wish, in the end you will be recompensed for them.” Qadi Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Salamah bin Ja’far bin Ali al-Qasai said: I found these additional words in these two hadiths: “Jibreel (peace be upon him) came and said: O Muhammad! (peace and blessings be upon him) Live as long as you wish, in the end you will have to die. Love whomever you wish, in the end you will have to part from them. And do whatever deeds you wish, in the end you will be recompensed for them.” Then he said: “O Muhammad! (peace and blessings be upon him) The honor of a believer is in his standing for prayer at night, and his dignity is in being independent of people.”"
"747","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrates from his father, who narrates from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Do good to the one who deserves it and to the one who does not deserve it, because if you do good to the one who deserves it, then you have done good to the right person, and if you do good to the one who does not deserve it, then (in that case) you yourself were deserving of it."
"748","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: ""O hardship! Go as far as you wish (eventually, by itself) you will go away."
"749","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), and there was a heap of dates with him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Bilal! What is this?"" He replied: ""O Messenger of Allah! This is for you and your guests."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you not fear that this may become smoke of the fire of Hell for you? Bilal! Spend (it) and do not fear any decrease from the One who is the Owner of the Throne."
"750","It is narrated from Masruq that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""O Bilal! Feed us."" So he brought a handful of dates. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Give us more."" So he gave you more (dates). The Prophet said: ""Give us more."" So he said: O Messenger of Allah! There is nothing else except these, and even these I had collected for you. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""O Bilal! Spend, and do not fear decrease from the One who is above the Throne."
"751","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give glad tidings of complete light on the Day of Resurrection to those who walk towards the mosques in the darkness of the night."
"752","Sayyiduna Buraidah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give glad tidings of complete light on the Day of Resurrection to those who walk towards the mosques in the darkness of the night."
"753","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give glad tidings of complete light on the Day of Resurrection to those who walk to the mosques in the darkness of the night."
"754","Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from his father, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), Sayyiduna Zaid bin Harithah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give glad tidings of complete light on the Day of Resurrection to those who walk towards the mosques in the darkness of the night."
"755","Sayyiduna Buraidah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Give glad tidings of complete light on the Day of Resurrection to those who walk towards the mosques in the darkness of the night."
"756","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give glad tidings of complete light on the Day of Resurrection to those who walk towards the mosques in the darkness of the night."
"757","Taliq bin Habib narrated this hadith in a concise form as marfu‘: “Marry a religious woman, may your hands be dust-covered.”"
"758","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Adhere to those deeds which you are able to do, for Allah does not tire, but you tire. And indeed, the most beloved deeds to Allah are those which are done consistently, even if they are few.” And this hadith has been narrated by Muslim ibn Hajjaj with his chain from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), who reports it as marfu‘: “Adhere to those deeds which you are able to do, for Allah does not tire (of rewarding), but you tire (of performing deeds).”"
"759","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you weigh, weigh with a tilt (in favor of the buyer)."
"760","Sayyiduna ‘Adi bin Hatim (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “When an honorable person from any people comes to you, then honor him.”"
"761","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When an honorable person from any people comes to you, honor him."
"762","Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said: ""What brings you here?"" I said: O Messenger of Allah! I have come to accept Islam. He says that the Prophet spread his cloak for me and said: ""When an honorable person from any people comes to you, honor him."
"763","Musa bin Anas narrates from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""When someone comes to meet you, honor him."
"764","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated it briefly: ""When you become angry, remain silent."
"765","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any one of you loves his brother, he should inform him."
"766","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “When any one of you loves his brother, he should inform him.”"
"767","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith: ""When allegiance is pledged to two caliphs, then kill the latter of them."
"768","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith: ""When any one of you desires something, he should see what he is desiring, because he does not know what may be written for him from his desire."
"769","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith: ""Whoever adopts moderation will not be in need."
"770","This narration is also reported through another chain from Ibrahim Hijri with his chain in a similar manner."
"771","Sayyiduna Ibn Mas‘ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Allah never grants honor because of ignorance, never humiliates because of forbearance, and wealth is never decreased by giving charity.”"
"772","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Mercy is only taken away from a wretched person."
"773","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d Sa’idi (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “A servant is never unsuccessful due to consultation, and is never successful due to neglecting opinion.” Allah the Exalted says: « وَشَاوِرْهُمْ فِي الْأَمْرِ » “And consult them in the matter.” And Allah the Exalted has said: « وَأَمْرُهُمْ شُورَىٰ بَيْنَهُمْ » “And their affairs are (decided) by mutual consultation among them.”"
"774","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever performs istikhara will not fail, and whoever consults (others) will not regret, and whoever adopts moderation will not become destitute.” Imam Tabarani said: Only Abdul Quddus has narrated it from Hasan, and his son is unique in narrating from him."
"775","Sayyiduna Suhaib (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""He does not believe in the Qur'an who considers its prohibited things to be lawful."
"776","Sayyiduna Suhaib (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say... and he narrated this hadith."
"777","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “He does not believe in the Qur’an who considers its prohibited things to be lawful.”"
"778","Sayyiduna Suhaib (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""He does not believe in the Qur'an who considers its prohibited things to be lawful."
"779","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""No provision more vast and ample has been given to a servant than patience."
"780","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) says that my family sent me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He says: I came at a time when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was addressing the people, so I heard him say: ""No provision has been given to a servant more ample and vast than patience."
"781","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Charity, wherever it is mixed with wealth, destroys that (wealth)."
"782","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (peace be upon him) . . . . . and she reported this hadith. Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal says: My father said: Its meaning is that a prosperous or wealthy person takes charity or zakat (and mixes it with his wealth), even though this charity is for the poor."
"783","Sayyida Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Charity does not decrease wealth, and when a servant forgives oppression and excess, Allah only increases his honor.”"
"784","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have not left any trial more harmful to men after me than women."
"785","Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have not left any trial more harmful to men after me than women."
"786","Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Saeed bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) both narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""I have not left any trial more harmful to men after me than women."" Or as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said."
"787","Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have not left any trial more harmful to men after me than women."
"788","Abu Nasirah reports that he met a slave of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), so he said: Have you heard anything from Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him)? He replied: Yes, I heard Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks forgiveness has not persisted (in the sin), even if he repeats (that sin) seventy times in a day."
"789","Ibn Shihab says that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The better charity a servant gives, Allah appoints equally good heirs over his estate."
"790","Ibn Shihab says that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said... and he narrated this hadith."
"791","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""I have not seen any (frightening) place like Hell from which the one fleeing is asleep (in heedlessness), nor have I seen any (blissful) place like Paradise whose seeker is asleep (in heedlessness)."
"792","A narration similar to this is also reported from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) through another chain of transmission."
"793","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whatever gentleness is found in, it beautifies it, and whatever harshness is found in, it makes it ugly.”"
"794","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever indecency is found in a thing, it makes it ugly, and whatever modesty is found in a thing, it makes it beautiful."
"795","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the sight of Allah, the only servant who is disgraced and insignificant is the one who is deprived of knowledge and manners."
"796","Hilal bin Yasaf narrates that during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), a man was wounded, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Call a physician for him."" The companions (may Allah be pleased with them) submitted: O Messenger of Allah! Can a physician benefit him in any way? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Yes, Allah has not sent down any disease except that He has also sent down its cure."
"797","Abu Ja'far Muhammad bin Ali says that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said... and he narrated this hadith: ""Allah Almighty has not adorned a servant with any adornment greater than heedfulness in his religion and chastity regarding his private parts."
"798","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah increases His blessings upon a servant, the needs of the people from him also increase."
"799","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said . . . . . . and he narrated this hadith."
"800","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever's sins Allah conceals in this world, He will not disgrace him for those (sins) on the Day of Resurrection."
